{"finding":{"specification":"CipherSpec","message":"the key given to Cipher.init carries a key-origin predicate the rule does not admit","class":"org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor.EncryptedKey","method":"encrypt","joint_findings":[]},"confirmed_cause":"The reported required-predicate violation is confirmed: the governed AES/GCM Cipher.init receives a caller-supplied key that failed CipherSpec's accepted key-origin predicate in observed executions (CLM-001, CLM-006). The bounded production callers supply either an AndroidKeyStore key or a PBKDF2-derived SecretKey (CLM-004, CLM-005), but the measured runs do not map a failing value to one specific source. Separately, the same AES-GCM initialization supplies only mode and key, while the verified rule requires preparedGCM parameters for GCM; this is an additional required-predicate specification violation. The provider-generated nonce uniqueness question remains unresolved and is not used to dismiss either predicate violation.","plan_invariants":["Existing EncryptedKey records remain decryptable using their persisted transformation, plaintext-key algorithm AAD, ciphertext, and encoded Cipher parameters (CLM-002, CLM-003).","The AndroidKeyStore-backed key in Encryptor remains resolvable for records created by the established lifecycle (CLM-004, CLM-005).","The PBKDF2-derived SecretKey in MasterKey remains resolvable for records created by the established lifecycle (CLM-004, CLM-005).","Newly written records use a persistent generated current wrapping key whose identity is retained sufficiently to reload that key for decryption (CLM-004, CLM-005, CLM-006).","Every current AES-GCM encryption uses fresh prepared GCM parameters/nonces, retains those parameters with the record, authenticates the same plaintext-key algorithm identifier as AAD, and decrypts with the retained parameters and AAD (CLM-001, CLM-002, CLM-003).","Existing EncryptedKey entry-point names remain available to current callers; record-version and key-selection details remain internal to the encryptor lifecycle (CLM-004)."],"plan_forbidden_changes":["Do not replace an existing wrapping key with an unpersisted transient generated key; records must remain recoverable across process restarts.","Do not remove or reinterpret legacy stored transformation strings, plaintext-key algorithm AAD, ciphertext, or encoded Cipher parameters (CLM-002, CLM-003).","Do not remove the existing EncryptedKey public entry points or require existing callers to change their entry-point names.","Do not change existing test assertions or encoded-key equality expectations to accommodate the migration.","Do not use a fixed, reused, or discarded AES-GCM nonce or parameter value.","Do not add build-file dependencies solely to support the migration or its tests."],"adjudication_concerns":[{"kind":"Persisted encrypted-record/key continuity","description":"The patch must preserve decryption of records encrypted with the existing AndroidKeyStore or PBKDF2-derived wrapping-key lifecycle, including records persisted before a change. The representation retains Cipher parameters, but the supplied evidence does not establish a self-describing wrapping-key identity or a legacy-key fallback contract."},{"kind":"Maintainer approval of key-lifecycle semantics","description":"A reviewer must approve the chosen key generation, storage, recovery, rotation, and migration behavior for both production caller paths. This decision is not settled by bounded source evidence or automated validation."},{"kind":"Provider/device GCM behavior","description":"If the review patch makes GCM nonce generation or GCMParameterSpec use explicit, it must be validated on supported Android providers and devices for encryption/decryption interoperability and fresh-nonce behavior. The pipeline does not run instrumentation tests or device/provider checks."}],"co_reported_findings":[],"previous_regressions":["Generating a new MasterKey through the public MasterKey.generate API.: before, The method derived a PBKDF2 software key and used the legacy EncryptedKey.encrypt overload, whose provider-generated GCM parameters allowed MasterKey generation to complete.; after the patch, MasterKey.generate creates or reloads currentMasterKey with randomized encryption required, then calls the three-argument EncryptedKey.encrypt overload, which passes a caller-generated GCMParameterSpec to Cipher.init. AndroidKeyStore rejects that initialization; the overload wraps the InvalidAlgorithmParameterException as InvalidKeyException, so generation fails after the alias may have been created.","Encrypting a token through Encryptor.encryptToken in an established lifecycle where the prior AndroidKeyStore master wrapping key permitted the original encryption path.: before, The method resolved the established masterKey alias and initialized AES-GCM without caller-supplied parameters, allowing the provider to generate encryption parameters and the encrypted token key to be written.; after the patch, Encryptor.encryptToken creates or reloads currentMasterKey and invokes the three-argument EncryptedKey.encrypt overload with an explicit caller-generated GCM nonce. The AndroidKeyStore key requires randomized encryption, so Cipher.init rejects those supplied GCM parameters and encryptToken fails with InvalidKeyException.","Decrypting a newly generated MasterKey with a password other than the password passed to MasterKey.generate.: before, The method derived the wrapping key from the supplied password and AES-GCM authentication failed when the derived key did not match the password-derived key used to encrypt the record.; after the patch, For a discriminator-bearing current record, MasterKey.decrypt(PBEKeySpec) bypasses SecretKeyFactory.generateSecret(spec) and decrypts solely with currentMasterKey. Thus any supplied password, including an incorrect one, returns the wrapped secret key while that AndroidKeyStore alias remains available."],"maintainer_responses_to_this_rule_elsewhere":[],"edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKey.java","symbol":"EncryptedKey.encrypt and the corresponding encrypted-record decryption/serialization paths","original_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
import java.security.InvalidAlgorithmParameterException;
import java.security.InvalidKeyException;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;

import javax.crypto.BadPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.IllegalBlockSizeException;
import javax.crypto.NoSuchPaddingException;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;

public final class EncryptedKey {
    private final byte[] mCipherText;
    private final byte[] mParameters;
    private final String mCipher;
    private final String mToken;

    private EncryptedKey(Cipher cipher, SecretKey token)
            throws BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        mCipher = cipher.getAlgorithm();
        mToken = token.getAlgorithm();

        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        mCipherText = cipher.doFinal(token.getEncoded());
        mParameters = cipher.getParameters().getEncoded();
    }

    public static EncryptedKey encrypt(SecretKey key, SecretKey plaintext)
            throws NoSuchAlgorithmException, NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException {
        if (key == null) {
            throw new InvalidKeyException("Key is null");
        }
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return new EncryptedKey(cipher, plaintext);
    }

    public SecretKey decrypt(SecretKey key)
            throws NoSuchPaddingException, NoSuchAlgorithmException, BadPaddingException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, IOException, InvalidAlgorithmParameterException,
            InvalidKeyException {
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance(mCipher);
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        String algorithm = cipher.getParameters().getAlgorithm();

        AlgorithmParameters ap = AlgorithmParameters.getInstance(algorithm);
        ap.init(mParameters);

        cipher.init(Cipher.DECRYPT_MODE, key, ap);
        cipher.updateAAD(mToken.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        return new SecretKeySpec(cipher.doFinal(mCipherText), mToken);
    }
}
","corrected_code":"package org.fedorahosted.freeotp.encryptor;

import android.util.Log;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;
import java.security.AlgorithmParameters;
